.TH NOUS 1 "2026-08-06" "nous 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nous \- see a folder of linked notes as a graph
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nous
[\fIdir\fR]
.br
.B nous
.I command
[\fIargs\fR]
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nous
reads every markdown file under a directory, follows the
.B [[wikilinks]]
and relative markdown links between them, and serves the result as a force graph
on localhost. One node per note, sized by how many links it has, coloured by a
frontmatter field of your choosing.
.PP
The page is re-read from disk on every request, so refreshing the browser shows
the vault as it is now. Nothing is written to the vault and nothing leaves the
machine.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B nous [\fIdir\fR]
Serve the vault and open it in a browser. With no argument, serves the directory
named by
.B dir
in the config.
.TP
.B build [\fIfile\fR]
Write a standalone HTML file with the graph inlined, default
.IR graph.html .
The file has no dependencies and no network calls, so it can be opened or sent
anywhere.
.TP
.B themes
List installed themes. The active one is marked.
.TP
.B config
Show the resolved settings and the paths they came from.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
Port to serve on. Default 4321; if it is busy nous climbs until it finds a free
one, up to 20 above.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Use this theme for one run, instead of the configured one.
.TP
.BI \-\-group\-by " FIELD"
Colour by this frontmatter field, or by the literal
.B folder
to use the top-level folder instead.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Do not open a browser.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output. Accepted by
.BR build ", " themes " and " config .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ~/.config/nous/config.toml
is written on first run:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dir = "."
group_by = "type"      # a frontmatter field, or "folder"
exclude = []           # globs, against the path inside the vault
theme = "spider-verse"
port = 4321
unresolved = false     # draw links to notes that do not exist

[physics]
repel = 5200
link_length = 190
link_strength = 0.0075
center = 0.00035
damping = 0.86
.fi
.RE
.PP
Set
.B NOUS_CONFIG
to use a different config directory.
.PP
An index note that links to every other note is worth putting in
.BR exclude :
it renders as a single hub with a spoke to everything and flattens the structure
you were trying to see.
.SH THEMES
Themes are TOML files in
.IR ~/.config/nous/themes/ .
The file name is the theme name. A theme carries the palette
.RB ( [colors] ),
one colour per value of the
.B group_by
field
.RB ( [groups] ,
with a
.B cycle
list for values it does not name), and the look
.RB ( [feel] :
.BR node_scale ,
.BR label_size ,
.BR link_opacity ,
.BR glow ,
.BR halftone ,
and
.BR duotone ,
a pair of colours printed slightly out of register behind each node, or
.B false
to switch it off).
.PP
.B spider\-verse
is written out on first run. Copy it to make your own.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
.TP
.B build \-\-json
.B {file, bytes, notes, links}
.TP
.B themes \-\-json
An array of
.BR {name, title, variant, active} .
.TP
.B config \-\-json
The resolved config, plus
.BR dir ", " config_file " and " themes_dir .
.SH KEYS
In the browser: drag to pan, scroll to zoom,
.B f
to refit the view, click a node to open it,
.B Escape
to close the panel. Dragging a node pulls it and lets the rest settle around it.
.PP
Under the filter box, the
.B Display
and
.B Forces
sections hold sliders for the theme's
.B [feel]
knobs and the config's
.B [physics]
values. They edit the running graph only; a refresh returns to what the files
say.
.PP
The two buttons under
.B Forces
replay the graph from an empty canvas over about six seconds, one note at a time.
.B animate \(bu links
grows it outward from the busiest note, so each note appears beside one it links
to.
.B animate \(bu time
brings them in by file modification time, which is the order the vault was
written in \(em though a vault that was cloned rather than written in place has
every file stamped at checkout, and falls back to the link order.
Panning or zooming during a replay stops the view refitting itself.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nous/config.toml
.TP
.I ~/.config/nous/themes/
.SH EXIT STATUS
Non-zero on a missing directory, an unreadable config, an unknown theme, or no
free port.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swatch (1)
